{
  // Dependency-vulnerability gate for CI (replaces the bare `npm audit --audit-level=high`,
  // which has no way to record a reasoned exception).
  //
  // The gate stays sharp: anything high/critical that is NOT listed below fails the build.
  // `allowlist` is per-advisory (GHSA id), never per-severity — we do not lower the level.
  //
  // Adding an entry requires, in this file: (1) the advisory id, (2) why it does not apply to
  // THIS codebase, measured — not assumed, (3) an expiry date, (4) what removes the need for it.
  // An expired entry is a task, not a renewal: re-check it, do not extend it by reflex.
  //
  // Policy: docs/development/dependency-audit.md
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "moderate": false,
  "high": true,
  "critical": true,
  "allowlist": [
    // GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action Execution Before
    // 400 Response" (high). Vulnerable range 7.12.0–8.2.0; there is NO fix in the 7.x line
    // (react-router-dom stops at 7.18.1; the fix is react-router v8 >= 8.2.1, a different
    // package and a breaking upgrade).
    //
    // Why it does not apply to payout (measured 2026-07-29, on this tree):
    //   - The admin console is a **static SPA built by Vite** (`npm run build` = `vite build`,
    //     no SSR entry) and served from `public_html/`. `src/main.tsx` mounts with
    //     `createRoot(...).render(...)`; there is no `hydrateRoot` / `renderToString` /
    //     `renderToPipeableStream` anywhere in `src/` (grep: 0 hits).
    //   - Routing is the **declarative** API — `<BrowserRouter>` + `<Routes>` in `src/App.tsx`
    //     and `src/app/router.tsx`. `createBrowserRouter` / data routers are not used, so there
    //     are no route-level `action:` / `loader:` definitions at all (grep for
    //     `^\s*(action|loader)\s*:` in `src/` matches only audit-log domain fields, never a
    //     route config object).
    //   - No RSC and no server runtime: grep for `react-router/server`, `@react-router/dev`,
    //     `'use server'`, `createStaticHandler`, `createStaticRouter` in `src/` = 0 hits.
    // The advisory's attack path (a server executing a route action before returning 400) has
    // no counterpart in a client-only bundle with no data-router actions.
    //
    // Expiry: 2026-08-31. Removed by the react-router v8 migration wave (bundled with the
    // NENE2 RR8 re-evaluation). If that wave slips past the expiry, the entry must be
    // re-argued in a PR — not silently extended.
    "GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2",

    // GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (brace-expansion) was here until 2026-08-05 (#277). It is now
    // REMOVED, not renewed: the entry's own stated removal condition — "an upstream 1.x
    // backport" — arrived as **brace-expansion 1.1.18**. `"brace-expansion@1": "^1.1.18"`
    // in overrides takes it, and because that stays inside the 1.x major it keeps the
    // `module.exports = expand` shape `minimatch@3.1.5` calls, so the #261 regression
    // (`TypeError: expand is not a function`) does not come back. Verified on this tree:
    //   node -e "require('.../jsx-a11y/node_modules/minimatch/minimatch.js').braceExpand('{a,b}c')"
    //   → [ 'ac', 'bc' ]
    // and the only two copies are 5.0.9 (hoisted) and 1.1.18 (under eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y),
    // both patched. audit-ci confirms independently: "Consider not allowlisting advisory:
    // GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg."
  ],
}
